{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1139352-updating-ready-made-characters-for-gmc-cod","id":1139352,"title":"Updating Ready-Made Characters for GMC/CoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-10T21:45:23-07:00","id":1139352,"title":"Updating Ready-Made Characters for GMC/CoD?","content":"Would anyone be interested in writing up versions of the various Ready-Made Characters (specifically base, Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, &amp; Promethean for now) that will fly with the 2013+ rules updates?<br /> <br /> As well as possibly premade PCs of their own design?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12476-voltron64","name":"Voltron64","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T02:37:25-07:00","id":1139386,"title":"","content":"I haven't bothered buying them, so I can't help too much directly.<br /> <br /> For the most part, base, Vampire, and Mage are pretty simple to convert.<br /> <br /> You need to check the new Virtue/Vice analogs (instead of the seven of each, though for base you can keep the old ones) for what would be appropriate replacements. Check Merits for any changes to ratings (generally are going to be cheaper if there's a change, or might have been eliminated). Adjust Defense and equipment as needed. A starting character's Integrity/equivalent is generally set at start. And then for the most part 2e adds stuff. So you need to add Aspirations, vampires will need a Touchstone, mages a Praxis spell, etc. Attributes and Skills are all essentially the same, Disciplines and Arcana distributions should be close enough. Etc.<br /> <br /> Werewolf and Promethean are a bit more work to convert due to the reworking of how their powers are handled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T10:56:23-07:00","id":1139484,"title":"","content":"I've scribbled notes on the 2e anchors of... well, not any of the RMCs, but the characters included in various 1e print books. (To Frances Black, for instance, I gave a Jester Mask and a Scholar Dirge.) For characters from <b>Promethean</b> books, I also worked out what Alembics are represented by their 1e Transmutations, and even made notes about what Roles they might have been through to have had the chance to calcify them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1426-aberranteyes","name":"AberrantEyes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T18:34:47-07:00","id":1139806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AberrantEyes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1139352-updating-ready-made-characters-for-gmc-cod?p=1139484#post1139484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've scribbled notes on the 2e anchors of... well, not any of the RMCs, but the characters included in various 1e print books. (To Frances Black, for instance, I gave a Jester Mask and a Scholar Dirge.) For characters from <b>Promethean</b> books, I also worked out what Alembics are represented by their 1e Transmutations, and even made notes about what Roles they might have been through to have had the chance to calcify them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do admit, Mask/Dirges, aspirations and touchstones are the hardest part for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12476-voltron64","name":"Voltron64","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}